description:
Change under review: show a preview of a link that a user pastes into a chat message. Added files are shown in full.

`src/preview/fetch-preview.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { lookup } from "node:dns/promises";
2 import { isPrivateAddress } from "../net/ip.js";
3 import { extractTitle, readTextCapped } from "./html.js";
4
5 export async function fetchPreview(rawUrl: string): Promise<string> {
6   const url = new URL(rawUrl);
7   if (url.protocol !== "https:") throw new Error("https only");
8   const { address } = await lookup(url.hostname);
9   if (isPrivateAddress(address)) throw new Error("private address");
10   const res = await fetch(url, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000) });
11   const body = await readTextCapped(res, 65_536);
12   return extractTitle(body) ?? body.slice(0, 300);
13 }
```

`src/routes/preview.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { requireSession } from "../auth/session.js";
2 import { fetchPreview } from "../preview/fetch-preview.js";
3
4 export const preview = requireSession(async (req) => {
5   const { url } = await req.json();
6   return Response.json({ preview: await fetchPreview(String(url)) });
7 });
```

`readTextCapped` is an existing helper that stops reading the body after the given number of bytes. `isPrivateAddress` is existing, tested code that rejects loopback, RFC 1918, link-local (including `169.254.169.254`) and their IPv6 equivalents. The service runs on a cloud VM whose metadata endpoint, `http://169.254.169.254/`, returns temporary cloud credentials. Anyone who signs up can post chat messages. Existing middleware enforces CSRF protection on every state-changing route: the session cookie is `SameSite=Strict`, and a request without a valid `X-CSRF-Token` header is rejected.
